<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cairn increases stake in Command Pet.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cairn increases stake in Command Pet.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cairn Energy Plc's Australian unit said it had increased its stake in its takeover target, Command Petroleum Ltd, to 106.76 million shares or about 33 percent of Command's ordinary shares.</p>
<p>Cairn is offering A$1.10 cash per share or two Cairn shares for every 13 Command shares.</p>
<p>Command's major shareholder, Snyder Oil Corp, said on November 7 it would accept for its 32.6 percent stake.</p>
<p>By 1.20 p.m. (0220 GMT), Command shares were a cent lower at A$1.12 on turnover of 9.5 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
